 If nothing is scheduled, use the Performance Center as a campus landmark on your walk.","short_summary":"A campus performance venue used for university arts programming.","evidence_claim":"Saint Mary’s identifies Joseph Page Theatre in the Performance Center, and its 2026 Shakespeare Showcase took place there with free general admission and required reservations.","source_url":"https://www.smumn.edu/newsroom/saint-marys-university-partners-with-great-river-shakespeare-festival-for-student-showcase/","source_title":"Saint Mary’s University partners with Great River Shakespeare Festival for student showcase","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2026-02-23","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Event availability, admission, and reservations vary; confirm the current listing before making plans.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"smumn-david-r-thies-arena","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"David R. Thies B’59 Arena","title":"Walk by David R. Thies B’59 Arena","subtitle":"Friday evening · campus athletics","notes":"Use the arena as a waypoint on an after-dinner campus loop. Check the university’s athletics or events calendar if you want to pair the walk with a scheduled activity.","short_summary":"The renamed Winona campus gymnasium is a major athletics landmark.","evidence_claim":"Saint Mary’s announced that its Winona campus gymnasium would be named the David R. Thies B’59 Arena.","source_url":"https://www.smumn.edu/newsroom/alumnus-leaves-lasting-mark-on-saint-marys/","source_title":"Alumnus leaves lasting mark on Saint Mary’s","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-05-07","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Building access and event entry depend on current university scheduling and policies.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"smumn-leo-ochrymowycz-memorial-soccer-field","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Leo Ochrymowycz Memorial Soccer Field","title":"Spot the soccer field on a campus loop","subtitle":"Saturday morning · outdoor campus stop","notes":"Take a daylight walk past the field and nearby athletic facilities. Keep to established campus routes and use the campus map to connect this stop with the rest of your loop.","short_summary":"A named outdoor athletic field on the Winona campus.","evidence_claim":"Saint Mary’s Winona campus map labels the Leo Ochrymowycz Memorial Soccer Field among its outdoor recreation facilities.","source_url":"https://international.smumn.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/28/2025/06/Win_CampusMap.pdf","source_title":"Saint Mary’s University of Minnesota Winona Campus Map","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View from public campus routes; field access depends on athletics scheduling.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"winona-lake-winona-path","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Lake Winona Path","title":"Take a Lake Winona Path walk","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · Lake Park","notes":"Choose a comfortable out-and-back segment for a first visit. Stay alert for pedestrians, skaters, and cyclists sharing the paved route, then turn around before dark.","short_summary":"A paved loop around East and West Lake Winona for walking or cycling.","evidence_claim":"The City of Winona describes Lake Winona Path as a five-mile blacktop trail through Lake Park that circles both lake segments and is used by pedestrians, skaters, and cyclists.","source_url":"https://www.winonamn.gov/780/Outdoor-Recreation","source_title":"Outdoor Recreation | City of Winona","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The city advises users to be alert because the path is shared by multiple types of travelers.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"winona-garvin-heights-park","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Garvin Heights Park","title":"Save Garvin Heights for a daylight view","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · Winona blufftop","notes":"Go in daylight with water and suitable shoes. Use the city’s listed trailhead and steps information to decide whether the short uphill route fits your group’s comfort level.","short_summary":"A city park with blufftop views and hiking paths through native ecosystems.","evidence_claim":"The City of Winona says Garvin Heights Park has hiking paths, a blufftop view, and a 0.4-mile trail with 378 man-made steps on its upper portion.","source_url":"https://www.winonamn.gov/Facilities/Facility/Details/Garvin-Heights-Park-58","source_title":"Garvin Heights Park | City of Winona","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The city lists a paved parking area and public-use picnic tables; use the marked trailhead and check conditions before hiking.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"minnesota-marine-art-museum","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Minnesota Marine Art Museum","title":"Plan a water-inspired art stop","subtitle":"Sunday afternoon · 800 Riverview Drive","notes":"Check current gallery hours and admission before heading over. If Sunday works for your schedule, give yourself time to explore the museum rather than rushing through it.","short_summary":"A Winona museum with art focused on water and the surrounding river setting.","evidence_claim":"MMAM lists museum hours Tuesday through Sunday, its Winona address, and a $7 student general-admission price; it also offers free student admission on Thursdays.","source_url":"https://mmam.org/hours-admission-location","source_title":"Hours, Admission and Location | Minnesota Marine Art Museum","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Current hours are Tuesday–Sunday, 10 a.m.–5 p.m.; student admission is listed separately, so verify any changes before visiting.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"winona-county-history-center","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Winona County History Center","title":"End with local history at the Armory","subtitle":"Sunday afternoon · 160 Johnson Street","notes":"Set aside an unhurried final stop for exhibits and the lobby gallery. Check the History Center’s visit page before leaving campus for current exhibit and access updates.","short_summary":"A historical museum in Winona’s 1915 National Guard Armory.","evidence_claim":"The Winona County Historical Society says the History Center is located in the historic 1915 National Guard Armory at 160 Johnson Street and lists daily museum-exhibit hours.","source_url":"https://winonahistory.org/visit/","source_title":"Visit Our Museums | Winona County Historical Society","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":"2026-07-15","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The visit page lists daily 10 a.m.–4 p.m. hours and $3 student admission; confirm exhibits and hours before arrival.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
